OL,3,GNEWSAMum in hospice treated to brunch
OL,4,Asurprise from favourite cafe
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mother who was too ill to fulfill her
OL,7,Fspecial wish of eating at her favourite
OL,8,Fcafe with her daughter was treated to a
OL,9,Fspecial surprise - as the eatery
OL,10,Fdelivered brunch to her hospice.
OL,12,FJean Neal, an in-patient at Pendleside
OL,13,FHospice, had a number of wishes,
OL,14,Fincluding to have her favourite meal at
OL,15,FDempsey's Cafe in Burnley, Lancashire,
OL,16,Fwith her daughter Hayley.
OL,18,FHowever, a few days before she was set
OL,19,Fto go, it became clear that she would
OL,20,Fbe too ill to leave the hospice, so
OL,21,Finstead it was decided to bring the
OL,22,Fcafe to Jean.
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,404,400,260,160,0,100
